<!--
     SPDX-FileCopyrightText: The LineageOS Project
     SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

     This is a Wi-Fi only tablet, so the Wi-Fi resource overlay is load bearing:
     without it com.android.wifi.resources runs pure AOSP defaults, and a large
     number of the capability flags default to false.

     One overlay is enough. Stock carries every Lenovo value twice — once
     targeting com.android.wifi.resources and once targeting
     com.google.android.wifi.resources — because stock ships Google's
     ServiceWifiResourcesGoogle.apk. PixelOS builds the AOSP
     ServiceWifiResources.apk, and the two stock RRO sets were verified to hold
     byte-identical values, so only the AOSP target is needed here.

     ⚠️ Stock's WifiResTarget.apk / WifiResMainlineTarget.apk are gated on
     ro.boot.product.vendor.sku=sun and this board reports `tuna`, so they are
     not even installed on stock. (ro.board.platform IS sun — that is the
     platform family, a different naming axis from the vendor SKU.) Everything
     that lives only in those two — bridged SoftAP and the four multi-STA
     concurrency flags — therefore resolves false on stock as well, and is
     deliberately not carried here. Verified three ways on the running device:
     `cmd overlay lookup`, `cmd wifi get-softap-supported-features` omitting
     wifi_softap_bridged_ap_supported, and the absence of ADDITIONAL_STA_*
     feature bits.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
          package="com.android.wifi.resources.overlay.malbec">
    <overlay android:targetPackage="com.android.wifi.resources"
             android:targetName="WifiCustomization"
             android:isStatic="true"
             android:priority="1" />
</manifest>
